[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3543543696","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112879#issuecomment-3543543696","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112879","id":3543543696,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7TNi-Q","user":{"login":"rsubtil","id":6501975,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDE5NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6501975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil","html_url":"https://github.com/rsubtil","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-17T19:35:09Z","updated_at":"2025-11-17T19:35:09Z","body":"The `attach` request only works if an instance is already running from Godot. Otherwise, you should use `launch` for Godot to launch the project. Godot does propagate the error for DAP clients in order to make this more clear. However, due to some changes, the [`showUser` property was set to `false`](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/68410acc61fb9996aba544a615b3927fe78a643e/editor/debugger/debug_adapter/debug_adapter_types.h#L179), hence why VSCode is not giving any feedback as to what's wrong. All current errors should be shown to the user, so this needs to be changed to `true`.\n\nOn another related note, Godot's DAP debugger only works for GDScript, so it cannot be used to debug C#. The debug configuration should be different; check [here](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.0/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_basics.html#visual-studio-code) and, for instance, [this configuration](https://github.com/chickensoft-games/GodotGame/blob/main/.vscode/launch.json) by [Chickensoft](https://chickensoft.games/).\n\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3543543696/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3544180272","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112879#issuecomment-3544180272","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112879","id":3544180272,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7TP-Yw","user":{"login":"codingus-g","id":50211143,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMjExMTQz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50211143?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/codingus-g","html_url":"https://github.com/codingus-g","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codingus-g/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codingus-g/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codingus-g/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codingus-g/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codingus-g/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codingus-g/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codingus-g/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codingus-g/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codingus-g/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-17T22:49:01Z","updated_at":"2025-11-18T00:50:02Z","body":"Closing because DAP is unrelated to C#\nbut I still have questions, mainly I don't understand how to setup debugging in a way where I can run from Godot, and have VSCodium connect and hit breakpoints. Can you tell me if that is how it works in the proprietary VSCode?\nI was trying to make it work like this, but maybe I am simply trying to achieve something that is impossible?\nIf anyone is reading this, please respond. It is very discouraging to not be able to even start developing because the toolchain is just chaos. Outdated official examples of launch/tasks, no specific segment dedicated to VSCodium and its tools, \nnothing works as I expect. \nSo far I was only able to `build in vscodium > attach to it`, but it doesnt relay logs to Godot (they don't show up even in the vscodium term) , I am unable to hit breakpoints from Godot, or launch from it and have vscodium attach to it.\nI am confused as to how people who develop c# support use it. I don't understand how you achieve anything with the current state of it? Does it work for you differently? Do you have no problems?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3544180272/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3553840171","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112879#issuecomment-3553840171","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112879","id":3553840171,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7T00wr","user":{"login":"rsubtil","id":6501975,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDE5NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6501975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil","html_url":"https://github.com/rsubtil","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/